---
components: ["Coachmark", "CoachmarkBeacon"]
description: Coachmarks introduce one feature in a dismissible callout anchored to a pulsing beacon or to any control, for first-run onboarding.
---

<script>
  import { Box, Button, Coachmark, CoachmarkBeacon, Stack } from "carbon-components-svelte";
</script>

## Basic

Click the beacon to open the coachmark. It stays open while the user keeps working, until they close it, press <DocKbd label="Escape" />, or click outside it. The dialog is named by `titleText`.

| Do | Why |
| --- | --- |
| Show one coachmark per feature, once. | It interrupts, so repeated dismissal teaches users to ignore it. |
| Keep the body to a sentence or two. | The callout is 288 px wide. |
| Use [Toggletip](/components/Toggletip) for help that is always available. | A coachmark is first-run onboarding, and a toggletip is reference. |
| Don't open several coachmarks at once. | Only one dialog should compete for the user's attention. |

<Coachmark titleText="Export in bulk" align="bottom-start">
  <p>Select rows, then use the toolbar to export them together.</p>
</Coachmark>

## Alignment

Set `align` to place the coachmark relative to its target. `start` and `end` name inline sides above and below the target, so they swap in RTL. The default is `"bottom"`.

| Value | Placement |
| --- | --- |
| `"top"`, `"bottom"` | Centered on the target. |
| `"top-start"`, `"bottom-start"` | Aligned to the target's inline start. |
| `"top-end"`, `"bottom-end"` | Aligned to the target's inline end. |
| `"left"`, `"right"`, with `-start` or `-end` | Beside the target. |

The coachmark stays in view. Near a window edge, or the edge of a box that clips it, it flips to the side with room. A coachmark that a box with `overflow` would cut off opens in a portal. Inside a [Modal](/components/Modal) it always does. Set `portalTooltip` to `true` or `false` to override this.

<Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={10}>
  <Coachmark titleText="Top" align="top-start" beaconDescription="Show top coachmark">
    A coachmark above its target.
  </Coachmark>
  <Coachmark titleText="End" align="right" beaconDescription="Show end coachmark">
    A coachmark beside its target.
  </Coachmark>
</Stack>

## Custom target

### Existing control

Use the `"target"` slot to open the coachmark from a control you already have. Spread `triggerProps` on it, which sets `aria-haspopup`, `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls`, and call `toggle` on click.

<Coachmark titleText="Filters" align="bottom-start">
  <Button slot="target" kind="tertiary" size="small" let:triggerProps let:toggle {...triggerProps} on:click={toggle}>
    Filter
  </Button>
  Filter by owner or status.
</Coachmark>

### Overlay beacon

Set `overlay` on a `CoachmarkBeacon` to place it on the end and top corner of its positioned parent, so it can mark an existing control without a button inside a button. The coachmark's wrapper is that parent.

<Coachmark titleText="New" align="right-start">
  <svelte:fragment slot="target" let:triggerProps let:toggle>
    <Button kind="tertiary" size="small">Share</Button>
    <CoachmarkBeacon overlay iconDescription="Show what is new about Share" {...triggerProps} on:click={toggle} />
  </svelte:fragment>
  Share a view with a link.
</Coachmark>

## Actions

Use the `"actions"` slot for buttons in the footer. Focus moves to the element that matches `selectorPrimaryFocus` (default `"[data-modal-primary-focus]"`), then to the first form field, then to the close button. Set it to `null` to move no focus.

Focus moves into the coachmark only when the user opened it, through the target or from a control inside it. A coachmark that opens by itself on page load leaves focus where it is, so it never takes it from a form. There is no focus trap, so <DocKbd label="Tab" /> leaves the coachmark and it stays open.

<DocKbd label="Escape" /> closes the coachmark when focus is on its target or inside it, and focus returns to the target. Pressing <DocKbd label="Escape" /> in an unrelated field does not close it. Inside a [Modal](/components/Modal), the coachmark closes first. The close button and a click on the target also return focus to the target, and an outside click leaves focus where the user put it.

<Coachmark titleText="Saved views" align="bottom-start">
  Pick up where you left off.
  <svelte:fragment slot="actions">
    <Button size="small" data-modal-primary-focus>Open views</Button>
  </svelte:fragment>
</Coachmark>

## Events

`open` fires when the coachmark opens. Its `detail.trigger` is `"target"` when the user opened it through the target, and `"programmatic"` otherwise.

`close` reports what closed it. A close by the user fires before the coachmark closes, and `preventDefault()` keeps it open. A `"programmatic"` close fires after it closes and cannot be canceled.

| `detail.trigger` | Closed by |
| --- | --- |
| `"close-button"` | The close button. |
| `"escape-key"` | <DocKbd label="Escape" /> from inside the coachmark. |
| `"outside-click"` | A click outside the target and the dialog. |
| `"target"` | A click on the target while it was open. |
| `"action"` | `close()` from a slot, such as a button in `"actions"`. |
| `"programmatic"` | `open` set to `false`, or an ancestor [Modal](/components/Modal) closing. |

## Persisting dismissal

Keep a coachmark from returning once the user has seen it by saving the flag with [LocalStorage](/components/LocalStorage). Open it from `onMount`, after the storage has loaded, so a returning user never sees it flash. Test `!seen`, because `clearItem()` resets the bound value to `undefined`.

<FileSource src="/framed/Coachmark/CoachmarkPersisted" />

## Tour

A tour that spans several controls is one coachmark per stop, opened by the consumer. Set `focusOnOpen` so focus follows the user from one stop to the next, since the next coachmark is opened by code, not by the user.

<FileSource src="/framed/Coachmark/CoachmarkTour" />

A tab is itself a control, so a beacon inside one would nest a button in a button. For a stop on a tab, anchor the coachmark to an inert marker in the tab, set `portalTooltip` so the dialog is rendered outside the tab and out of its name, and open it from the tour.
